{"fileVersion":"1.0","metadata":{"title":"Twilite Graph Model","description":"A topic graph explaining Twilite's graph-native artifact model.","graphId":"twilite-graph-model","version":"1.0.1","kind":"documentation","created":"2026-09-17T16:11:00.000Z","modified":"2026-09-17T16:35:00.000Z","author":"","tags":["twilite","graph-model","documentation","topic"],"preferredViewer":"https://twilite.zone"},"nodes":[{"id":"twilite-graph-model-declaration","type":"declaration","label":"Twilite Graph Model Declaration","position":{"x":-900,"y":-1150},"width":420,"height":280,"ports":[{"id":"default-view","label":"default view","direction":"output","dataType":"any","angle":165},{"id":"summary-view","label":"summary view","direction":"output","dataType":"any","angle":180},{"id":"icon-view","label":"icon view","direction":"output","dataType":"any","angle":195},{"id":"glyph","label":"glyph","direction":"output","dataType":"any","angle":270},{"id":"landing-surface","label":"landing surface","direction":"output","dataType":"any","angle":0}],"visible":true,"showLabel":true,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model","name":"Twilite Graph Model","version":"1.0.1","description":"A topic graph explaining Twilite's graph-native artifact model."},"intent":{"kind":"documentation","scope":"public"},"dependencies":{"nodeTypes":["declaration","view","content","glyph","bridge","topic","topic-concept","topic-claim","topic-perspective","topic-source","topic-synthesis"],"portContracts":["core"],"skills":["topic-template"]},"authority":{"mutation":{"allowCreate":true,"allowUpdate":true,"allowDelete":true,"appendOnly":false},"actors":{"humans":true,"agents":true,"tools":true},"styleAuthority":"descriptive"},"settings":{"snapToGrid":false,"gridSize":20,"edgeRouting":"auto","autoSave":false,"layout":{"mode":"manual"}},"declaration":{"kind":"graph","targetMode":"artifact","artifactKind":"graph","interfaceContract":{"version":1,"implicitRootPort":true},"defaultSurfaceId":"default-view","surfaces":[{"id":"default-view","kind":"view","label":"Twilite Graph Model Detail","viewNodeId":"twilite-graph-model-detail-view"},{"id":"summary-view","kind":"view","label":"Twilite Graph Model Summary","viewNodeId":"twilite-graph-model-summary-view"},{"id":"icon-view","kind":"view","label":"Twilite Graph Model Icon","viewNodeId":"twilite-graph-model-icon-view"},{"id":"glyph","kind":"view","label":"Twilite Graph Model Glyph","viewNodeId":"twilite-graph-model-glyph"},{"id":"landing-surface","kind":"view","label":"Twilite Graph Model Landing","viewNodeId":"twilite-graph-model-landing-surface"}]},"document":{"url":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/topics/twilite-graph-model/root.node"}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-detail-view","type":"view","label":"Twilite Graph Model Detail","position":{"x":-1800,"y":-600},"width":680,"height":340,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210}],"handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":270,"portId":"root"}],"visible":true,"showLabel":true,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"},"content":{"kind":"markdown","value":"# Twilite Graph Model\n\nTwilite treats the **graph itself as the artifact**, not as hidden plumbing for a single application. A declaration states graph identity, intent, authority, dependencies, and exposed surfaces. **Ports** are semantic endpoints while **handles** are visual anchors. **Views**, **content**, and **glyphs** separate presentation from semantics. **Portals** compose graphs by durable address, and **bridges** import explicit class authority.\n\nThat separation gives people, renderers, editors, scripts, and agents one coherent structure to operate on."}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-summary-view","type":"view","label":"Twilite Graph Model Summary","position":{"x":-1860,"y":-1040},"width":560,"height":260,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210}],"handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":0,"portId":"root"}],"visible":true,"showLabel":true,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"},"content":{"kind":"markdown","value":"## Twilite Graph Model\n\n**Graph = artifact + interface + presentation + address.**\n\nDeclarations say what the graph is. Ports say how it connects. Handles say where those connections appear. Views/content/glyphs say how it presents. Portals open other graphs. Bridges import authority."}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-icon-view","type":"view","label":"Twilite Graph Model Icon","position":{"x":-1560,"y":-1480},"width":360,"height":240,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210}],"handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":90,"portId":"root"}],"visible":true,"showLabel":true,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"},"content":{"kind":"svg","value":"<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 320 220' role='img' aria-label='Twilite graph model'><rect width='320' height='220' rx='28' fill='#0f172a'/><circle cx='160' cy='110' r='35' fill='#60a5fa'/><circle cx='72' cy='62' r='18' fill='#34d399'/><circle cx='248' cy='62' r='18' fill='#f59e0b'/><circle cx='72' cy='164' r='18' fill='#a78bfa'/><circle cx='248' cy='164' r='18' fill='#fb7185'/><path d='M91 72 L131 94 M229 72 L189 94 M91 154 L131 126 M229 154 L189 126' stroke='#e2e8f0' stroke-width='6' stroke-linecap='round'/><text x='160' y='107' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a' font-family='system-ui' font-size='13' font-weight='900'>GRAPH</text><text x='160' y='124' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a' font-family='system-ui' font-size='12' font-weight='800'>MODEL</text></svg>"}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-glyph","type":"glyph","label":"Twilite Graph Model Glyph","position":{"x":-800,"y":-1480},"width":220,"height":180,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210}],"handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":90,"portId":"root"}],"visible":true,"showLabel":true,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"},"glyph":{"kind":"icon","name":"Network"}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-landing-surface","type":"content","label":"Twilite Graph Model Landing","position":{"x":360,"y":-700},"width":660,"height":280,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210}],"handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180,"portId":"root"}],"visible":true,"showLabel":true,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"},"content":{"kind":"markdown","value":"# A graph that knows what it is\n\nTwilite keeps **identity, semantics, presentation, navigation, and authority** distinct but connected. The graph remains the object as renderers, workspaces, agents, and spatial presentations change."}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-topic","type":"topic","label":"Topic","position":{"x":-100,"y":-160},"width":460,"height":320,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"title":"The Twilite Graph Model","description":"A graph-native model in which the graph is a self-describing artifact rather than an implementation detail hidden beneath an application.","scope":"Declarations, ports, handles, views, content, glyphs, portals, bridges, edges, and durable graph addressing.","definitionKey":"topic","_classBinding":{"key":"topic","sourceRef":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic.node-class.node"},"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-concept","type":"topic-concept","label":"Concept","position":{"x":-760,"y":260},"width":440,"height":300,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"title":"Graph-native artifact","definition":"The graph carries its own identity, intent, interface, presentation relationships, navigation boundaries, and authority.","notes":"The important distinctions are structural: declaration vs surface, port vs handle, view vs content, portal vs local ownership, and bridge authority vs a mere type string.","definitionKey":"topic-concept","_classBinding":{"key":"topic-concept","sourceRef":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-concept.node-class.node"},"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-claim","type":"topic-claim","label":"Claim","position":{"x":-260,"y":260},"width":440,"height":300,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"title":"The graph is the object","claim":"Twilite is strongest when applications, renderers, agents, and tools are ways of operating on a coherent graph rather than when the graph is reduced to an application-specific feature.","confidence":"high","definitionKey":"topic-claim","_classBinding":{"key":"topic-claim","sourceRef":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-claim.node-class.node"},"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-mechanism","type":"bridge","label":"Mechanism","position":{"x":240,"y":260},"width":460,"height":320,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],"handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180,"portId":"root"}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"title":"How the model stays coherent","description":"Host contribution to an extracted semantic fragment.","identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model","nodeId":"twilite-graph-model-mechanism"},"target":{"mode":"expand","kind":"graph","ref":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/topics/twilite-graph-model/how-model-stays-coherent.node","nodeId":"twilite-graph-model-mechanism","graphId":"twilite-graph-model-mechanism-fragment"},"bridge":{"ref":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/topics/twilite-graph-model/how-model-stays-coherent.node","kind":"graph","nodeId":"twilite-graph-model-mechanism","graphId":"twilite-graph-model-mechanism-fragment"},"authority":"bridge","extraction":{"role":"host-participant","createdAt":"2026-09-17T16:35:00.000Z","fragmentRef":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/topics/twilite-graph-model/how-model-stays-coherent.node"},"agentGuidanceRef":"/agent-guidance/fragment-authoring.md","presentation":{}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-perspective","type":"topic-perspective","label":"Perspective","position":{"x":760,"y":260},"width":460,"height":320,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"title":"Graph-first vs application-first","perspective":"An application-first system starts with a task and uses a graph to serve it. Twilite's graph-first approach starts with the graph as a general object and lets applications and workspaces emerge as projections and capabilities.","distinction":"The difference is not whether both use nodes and edges; it is which thing is treated as primary.","definitionKey":"topic-perspective","_classBinding":{"key":"topic-perspective","sourceRef":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-perspective.node-class.node"},"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-source","type":"topic-source","label":"Source","position":{"x":-260,"y":680},"width":460,"height":300,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"title":"Twilite graph contracts","citation":"github://twilite-zone/public/library/documentation/contracts/onboarding.md","notes":"The onboarding guide defines current primitive roles, graph-native composition, provider address semantics, and class-authority expectations. This graph is structurally derived from github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/root.node.","definitionKey":"topic-source","_classBinding":{"key":"topic-source","sourceRef":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-source.node-class.node"},"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-synthesis","type":"topic-synthesis","label":"Synthesis","position":{"x":300,"y":680},"width":560,"height":340,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"title":"Current Synthesis","summary":"Twilite's graph model is a self-describing artifact protocol. The graph says what it is, exposes semantic interfaces, separates presentation from connection geometry, composes remote graphs by durable address, and imports executable authority explicitly. That shared structure can then support browsing, editing, automation, agents, multi-graph workspaces, and future spatial renderers without redefining the object each time.","openQuestions":"How far can dynamic ports, derived instances, and 3D/VR projections expand while preserving the clean separation between semantics, presentation, navigation, and authority?","definitionKey":"topic-synthesis","_classBinding":{"key":"topic-synthesis","sourceRef":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-synthesis.node-class.node"},"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-bridge-topic","type":"bridge","label":"Topic Class Authority","position":{"x":-1300,"y":-240},"width":360,"height":180,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210}],"visible":true,"showLabel":true,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"},"bridge":{"ref":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic.node-class.node","role":"import","resourceKind":"node-class","scope":"focused-graph","grants":["read","create","update"]}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-bridge-topic-concept","type":"bridge","label":"Concept Class Authority","position":{"x":-1300,"y":0},"width":360,"height":180,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210}],"visible":true,"showLabel":true,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"},"bridge":{"ref":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-concept.node-class.node","role":"import","resourceKind":"node-class","scope":"focused-graph","grants":["read","create","update"]}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-bridge-topic-claim","type":"bridge","label":"Claim Class Authority","position":{"x":-1300,"y":240},"width":360,"height":180,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210}],"visible":true,"showLabel":true,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"},"bridge":{"ref":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-claim.node-class.node","role":"import","resourceKind":"node-class","scope":"focused-graph","grants":["read","create","update"]}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-bridge-topic-perspective","type":"bridge","label":"Perspective Class Authority","position":{"x":1300,"y":200},"width":360,"height":180,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210}],"visible":true,"showLabel":true,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"twilite-graph-model"},"bridge":{"ref":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-perspective.node-class.node","role":"import","resourceKind":"node-class","scope":"focused-graph","grants":["read","create","update"]}}},{"id":"twilite-graph-model-bridge-topic-source","type":"bridge","label":"Source Class Authority","positi